From 49a7acda0bf1074d8269ca22eee598febb827256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:39:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Cantilever Case 7: base on y = 0 as a second planar structure
 (plate, bar, inclined fork arms)

truss2d.fit finds face layers (the base on y = 0) and fits each in its own plane;
the face trusses stand on it. swtruss.py builds one sketch per structure (Truss
on the Front Plane, Base on the Top Plane), depths t and tb as global variables.
Fit fixes: pinholes filled, width-step split, joint merge by the narrower width,
joints only moved in directions their lines fix; geometry: bevels for nearly
straight joints, capped chord mitres, fillets skipped where they do not fit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BdLZZ8R4FqXDzDRWDvVnZQ
